# Independent counterexamples are labelled separately from the historical text.
C('8-009R',[16],'J156-8-02','330-339','Own audit of the unrestricted implication, not a quotation','Mog L1 does not imply Mog L2 for arbitrary magasins. Take four strata x,y,X,Y, incidence equality, open refinement x<X and y<Y, and disjointness only x⊥y,y⊥x. All original axioms and L1 hold; L2 fails for X,Y. This does not refute the author’s explicitly qualified expectation for unspecified practical examples.','proved in this run; reconstruction','magasins','Exact symbolic verification of every axiom in proof_audits.md §L.',confidence='high')
C('8-018R',[31],'J156-8-04','247','Own audit separating the two face-disjointness axioms','The comparable-face condition is strictly weaker than pairwise disjointness of all distinct faces of a common object, even with deployment injectivity. A five-stratum model has incidence a<b,c<b, identity open refinement, disjointness edges ab,cb,ad,ce; all other carrier/order axioms hold, deployments are distinct, but a and c are not disjoint. A requirement that deployments land in spatial figures would restore the missing condition implicitly.','proved in this run; reconstruction','magasins','Exact finite certificate in computations.py; proof_audits.md §D.',confidence='high')
C('8-030R',[64],'J156-8-08','126-154','Own counterexample to monotone elementary-value extension','An arbitrary monotone assignment of elementary figures need not extend to a compatible-join-preserving map, even with finite source and full target atlas: map the two elements of a discrete trivial two-stratum maquette to two distinct strata in a target with equality orders and empty disjointness. The source pair is a figure; the target pair is not. Compatibility of the images is therefore an additional necessary premise.','proved in this run; reconstruction','order','All axioms checked symbolically in proof_audits.md §G; finite data in computations_output.txt.',confidence='high')
C('9-030R',[63,64,65],'J156-9-08','168-283','Own counterexample and valid remaining inclusion','Disjointness preservation does not imply cl′(α[cl A])=cl′(α[A]): take source {a,b} with no disjoint pairs, target {u,v} with u⊥v, and a↦u,b↦v. For A={a}, the left side is {u,v} and right side {u}. For any disjointness-preserving correspondence, the weaker inclusion cl′(α[B⊥])⊆(α[B])⊥ always holds. The author’s nonsurjective-injection example independently refutes complement preservation.','proved in this run; reconstruction','orthomorphisms','Exact finite relation and polar enumeration in computations.py; proof_audits.md §C.',confidence='high')
